    icon: '💡',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "In a 1-card round, if you have a high trump (Ace or King), bid 1; otherwise, bid 0. As the hand size grows, evaluate your 'Safe Tricks' (Aces/Kings in short suits) and your 'Danger Tricks' (Queens/Jacks) which might win unexpectedly.\n\nThe 'Zero Bid' Defense: If you bid zero, your goal is to discard high cards as early as possible on other people's tricks. If you have a King and someone leads that suit, throw it on! Don't get stuck with high cards in the final tricks when you have no other choice but to win.\n\nSocial Manipulation (The Undercut): If the bids are 'Under' (total bids < tricks available), someone will be forced to win a trick they didn't want. Use this. If you bid 1 and you've already won your trick, start leading low cards in your long suits to force the opponents who wanted 0 tricks to win them.",
    Player: "In a 1-card round, if you have a high trump (Ace or King), bid 1; otherwise, bid 0. As the hand size grows, evaluate your 'Safe Tricks' (Aces/Kings in short suits) and your 'Danger Tricks' (Queens/Jacks) which might win unexpectedly.\n\nThe 'Zero Bid' Defense: If you bid zero, your goal is to discard high cards as early as possible on other people's tricks. If you have a King and someone leads that suit, throw it on! Don't get stuck with high cards in the final tricks when you have no other choice but to win.\n\nSocial Manipulation (The Undercut): If the bids are 'Under' (total bids < tricks available), someone will be forced to win a trick they didn't want. Use this. If you bid 1 and you've already won your trick, start leading low cards in your long suits to force the opponents who wanted 0 tricks to win them.",
    aggressiveness: 0.5,
    riskTolerance: 0.5,
