    basic: "In a 1-card round, if you have a high trump (Ace or King), bid 1; otherwise, bid 0. As the hand size grows, evaluate your 'Safe Tricks' (Aces/Kings in short suits) and your 'Danger Tricks' (Queens/Jacks) which might win unexpectedly.",
    intermediate: "The 'Zero Bid' Defense: If you bid zero, your goal is to discard high cards as early as possible on other people's tricks. If you have a King and someone leads that suit, throw it on! Don't get stuck with high cards in the final tricks when you have no other choice but to win.",
    advanced: "Social Manipulation (The Undercut): If the bids are 'Under' (total bids < tricks available), someone will be forced to win a trick they didn't want. Use this. If you bid 1 and you've already won your trick, start leading low cards in your long suits to force the opponents who wanted 0 tricks to win them.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "If you are the dealer and the total bids are currently equal to the tricks, you ARE 'The Hooked'. You must bid something else, forcing the table into unbalanced territory.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Don't bid 1 with a 'middling' card like a 7 or 8 unless it is a trump and the hand size is large.",
      },
